From 5f76d9469f1ccfe55b93a807808ee72f3bfeef89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:20:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-80: the property marker like WPF; reset to DFM
 always writes position / size (0.80.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"所有基礎操作模式能跟WPF一樣方便" (EastSun 20260930), part 8, from Microsoft's
"WPF and Silverlight Designer Overview" / "Create UIs ... > Properties window":
- the property marker: every row of 外觀與版面 compared with the .dfm has a small
  box right of its value -- hollow = the .dfm's value, filled = changed; a click
  opens its menu with 「重設（改回 DFM：…）」 (off when it is the same or the field
  cannot be edited). It replaces the ↺ that showed only on changed rows.
- reset to DFM (follows 0.78.0): the page moves a control by "the target minus
  what it shows", so a page that is behind the source (it showed 54 while the
  source said 60 -- seen in the real VS Code test) took "reset to 54" as "no
  change" and wrote nothing. The reset's position / size items now carry force:
  the page writes those px values even where it already shows them.
- vscode_it: select-same-type waits until spbSave alone is selected before
  asking (an unanswered selection left sbtExit as the primary) and says what it
  saw.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 159, smoke 166, panels, real VS Code 148): lib
(resetItemsOf gives force), probe (force writes the value the page already
shows; without force nothing), panels (9 markers, 1 filled = Font.Bold, a click
opens the menu without posting, Reset posts bold = false).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
